🟢🔵 Zero Downtime? Yes, Please!

Today’s DevOps Scenario: Blue-Green Deployment Using Jenkins + Ansible 🚀

If you’ve ever deployed an app to production and crossed your fingers 🤞… this one’s for you!

🎯 𝐒𝐜𝐞𝐧𝐚𝐫𝐢𝐨:

👉 Deploy to a Green environment while Blue stays live.
👉 Test thoroughly. ✅
👉 If all good → switch traffic from Blue to Green.
👉 If anything breaks → rollback instantly.

This is called 𝑩𝒍𝒖𝒆-𝑮𝒓𝒆𝒆𝒏 𝑫𝒆𝒑𝒍𝒐𝒚𝒎𝒆𝒏𝒕, and it’s how top teams deliver updates with zero downtime and maximum confidence.

👨💻 𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐥-𝐓𝐢𝐦𝐞 𝐅𝐥𝐨𝐰: 𝐉𝐞𝐧𝐤𝐢𝐧𝐬 + 𝐀𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐛𝐥𝐞

✔️ Jenkins pulls the latest code from GitHub

✔️ Ansible deploys it to the Green servers

✔️ Jenkins runs smoke tests (basic functionality check)

✔️ If tests pass → switch load balancer to Green

✔️ If tests fail → leave Blue running, alert team

🧠 𝐊𝐞𝐲 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐜𝐞𝐩𝐭𝐬 𝐂𝐨𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐞𝐝:

⚡Jenkins pipelines

⚡Ansible playbooks for app deployment

⚡Load balancer switch (Nginx/HAProxy/ALB)

⚡Instant rollback strategy 🔁

📘 𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐥 𝐄𝐱𝐚𝐦𝐩𝐥𝐞 (𝐒𝐢𝐦𝐩𝐥𝐢𝐟𝐢𝐞𝐝 𝐕𝐢𝐞𝐰)

🧹Jenkinsfile defines stages: checkout → deploy → test → switch

🧹Ansible handles the environment-specific config

